  "id": "COMPOUND:18043 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Arjunglucoside I appears to interact with CD276 antigen through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a complex network of molecular relationships. The evidence indicates that Arjunglucoside I directly targets VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of a compound with a structural similarity to (7E,9E,16Z)-18-hydroxyoctadeca-7,9,16-trien-11,13-diyn-4-one. This compound is also linked to CD276 antigen, implying a potential pathway involving lipid-based signaling. Additionally, Arjunglucoside I is shown to target Hepatocyte, which is a target of another compound with a different structural profile, also leading to CD276 antigen. These findings suggest that Arjunglucoside I may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the modulation of lipid metabolism or the activation of a signaling cascade that ultimately leads to CD276 antigen engagement. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Arjunglucoside I in influencing cellular processes that are associated with CD276 antigen activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
